      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, the veterinarian also informed DOHMH that, in his professional experience, the second most important factor for establishing a sound locomotive examination is to confirm through bloodwork that the horse being evaluated is not on any painkillers that would mask its unsoundness, and such bloodwork is commonly performed on working horses; and",
